{"artifacts":[],"checksum":"sha256:468f893185807578638a35749f28d43ef364f2b32d8a104bfcbe18ad5280f68b","events":[{"actor":{"id":"system-runtime","type":"system"},"artifactRefs":[],"eventHash":"sha256:c71f24026065da40cf52ce6e271851757f55be99512833d498e64f76aaa9cb5f","eventId":"event-325f9a42-80aa-4061-b31e-11cc954719e3","evidenceRefs":[{"ciphertextSha256":"bb7fefda7ed7c04d34b1e66f06d5457bfad743e06e7e01cfc3d3a48391d54368","contentSha256":"915478675ff2d9b57f92238dcbb49698e37bfc704a1d5f40a8eb4059a36bb644","evidenceId":"exec-exec-m08-judge-judge-a1-judgment"}],"idempotencyKey":"node-outcome-5c53b481-0798-4755-be1a-4096aad44cfe","kind":{"data":{"executionId":"exec-m08-judge","nextState":"failed","nodeId":"judge","outcome":"terminal_failure","reason":"judge_refused"},"type":"node_outcome_recorded"},"occurredAt":"2026-08-18T10:10:29.473801800Z","previousHash":"sha256:f579fc3c0b278ca5ba7af1a09ce0924d5f79ea5c84c1c6bf7f4a088c00d39ede","schemaVersion":"1.0.0","scope":{"executionId":"exec-m08-judge","projectId":"project-local","workspaceId":"workspace-local"},"sensitivity":"internal","sequence":14,"streamId":"exec-m08-judge"},{"actor":{"id":"system-runtime","type":"system"},"artifactRefs":[],"eventHash":"sha256:246360ce5b598af258a1c3aaa6a7b4c94d4dafe5ac040e92943afbc0bad67028","eventId":"event-0594eaec-a48e-4f41-b55a-483dc30ab342","evidenceRefs":[],"idempotencyKey":"gate-verdict-42276786-49fb-4447-81e9-a3f19847bdc8","kind":{"data":{"executionId":"exec-m08-judge","findings":[{"claim":"status asserts attentionRequired:false and attentionReasons:[] while the same payload reports silenceUnevaluated:[\"judge\"] — the all-clear is published before the silence check that would justify it has run. Node `judge` stayed in state `running` with zero content appends across 3+ minutes of observation (contentHead pinned at 12), i.e. a wedged execution renders as 'go back to sleep'.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Never emit attentionRequired:false while any lane is in silenceUnevaluated. Make the glance verdict tri-state (clear / unknown / attention) and default unevaluated lanes to 'unknown', with the lane name and the reason it is unevaluated carried in attentionReasons.","severity":"critical"},{"claim":"The one-glance surface hides a real failure. Node `flaky_check` recorded outcome retryable_failure (reason tool_exited_non_zero) at sequence 10 and dropped back to queued, yet status shows failed:0, attentionReasons:[], untriagedInterruptions:[] and no retry, attempt, or failure counter anywhere. The failure is discoverable only by reading the raw event ledger.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Add retry/failure counters to the status payload (e.g. attemptsByNode, retryingNodes, failuresSinceStart) and surface a repeat-failure threshold as an attentionReason so a flapping node escalates without the operator reading events.","severity":"high"},{"claim":"status carries no liveness or time signal — no lastEventAt, no node start/elapsed time, no heartbeat, no expected-duration. `running` at 10:05:53 and `running` three minutes later with no progress are byte-identical responses, so the operator cannot distinguish healthy work from a hang, which is exactly the judgment the story requires.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Include lastContentAppendAt, per-node enteredStateAt/elapsed, and a staleness threshold; raise an attentionReason such as node_stalled when a running node exceeds it.","severity":"high"},{"claim":"The wake contract is not predictable from its own replies. wake_arm(cursor:12) returned headSequence:13, implying the log had already moved past the cursor and the lease would ring; two wake_wait calls (60s, then 120s) both returned outcome timeout. wake_status revealed the ring actually keys on contentHead:12, a field wake_arm never returns.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Return contentHead (and whether the lease is already satisfied) from wake_arm, so an operator can tell at arm time whether the wait will ring immediately or block.","severity":"medium"},{"claim":"silenceUnevaluated is an opaque bare identifier list. It carries no reason, no severity, no expected-evaluation time and no suggested action, so the operator cannot tell whether it is benign bookkeeping or the reason the all-clear is unsafe.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Replace the string list with objects carrying nodeId, whySkipped, sinceWhen, and operatorAction, and reflect it in the top-level attention verdict.","severity":"medium"},{"claim":"events returns the raw hash-chained ledger — previousHash, eventHash, idempotencyKey, evidenceRefs, schemaVersion, scope on every record — with no digest, no severity filter and no since-last-glance view. Answering 'did anything go wrong' meant reading 13 verbose records to find one failure line.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Add a summary/digest mode (or a severity/kind filter) returning only outcome-bearing events in compact form, defaulting to events since the caller's wake cursor.","severity":"medium"},{"claim":"wake_wait's timeout reply is content-free to the point of uselessness for the sleep loop: {\"outcome\":\"timeout\",\"timeoutSeconds\":60} omits current head and cursor, forcing extra wake_status/status round-trips just to confirm nothing moved.","evidence":[],"remediation":"Include head, contentHead and cursor in the timeout reply so a no-op wake costs zero follow-up calls.","severity":"low"}],"gateId":"judge-usefulness","nodeId":"judge","passed":false},"type":"gate_verdict"},"occurredAt":"2026-08-18T10:10:29.473801800Z","previousHash":"sha256:c71f24026065da40cf52ce6e271851757f55be99512833d498e64f76aaa9cb5f","schemaVersion":"1.0.0","scope":{"executionId":"exec-m08-judge","projectId":"project-local","workspaceId":"workspace-local"},"sensitivity":"internal","sequence":15,"streamId":"exec-m08-judge"}],"evidenceIds":["exec-exec-m08-judge-judge-a1-judgment"],"expectedNextSequence":14,"formatVersion":"1.0.0","requestDigest":"sha256:588314c3ba23ec40a091fc86903af3d314d56c766e16e6267b9ce9fe398e15bf","scope":{"executionId":"exec-m08-judge","projectId":"project-local","workspaceId":"workspace-local"},"streamId":"exec-m08-judge"}
